spoint editor fly-cam freelook was DEAD for two stacked reasons (both fixed). (1) camera.js update() editMode branch builds its lookAt from yaw/pitch but RETURNED before the yaw-=inputYawDelta / pitch-=inputPitchDelta apply+decay lines that only run in the gameplay branch below -> look deltas never applied in editor. FIX: apply+decay inputYaw/PitchDelta (with the same inputSmoothHz exp smoothing + pitchMin/Max clamp) INSIDE the editMode branch before the lookAt. (2) NO input source: cam.onMouseMove only attaches under pointer lock (app.js pointerlockchange) and entering edit mode EXITS pointer lock, so movementX/Y never reached the cam. FIX: cam.editLook(dx,dy) method feeds the delta accumulators; app.js wires a RIGHT-button drag on the canvas (mousedown btn2 + cam.getEditMode -> window mousemove -> cam.editLook; mouseup releases). A RMB press that moves >0 sets _flyMoved which suppresses the editor contextmenu (create-box/prop menu) so look-drag doesn't pop the menu; a plain RMB click still opens it. LMB stays gizmo/pick. Witnessed browser-3/14: TOGGLE_EDITOR + cam.editLook(150,60) -> yaw 0->-0.21 pitch seed-0.2->-0.287, yawChanged/pitchChanged true. NOTE: reading cam.getEditMode() right after via page.evaluate can return false (timing) even though the editMode branch ran - trust the yaw/pitch mutation (only the editMode branch mutates them) over the getEditMode snapshot.